      "recommended_risk": "low",
      "technical_explanation": "The reconcile step references wevm/frog/reconcile@v1 using a floating major-version tag for a third-party action. A tag retag or upstream compromise would let arbitrary code run in a job that has contents write and id-token write permissions. SHA-pinning would eliminate the tag-movement risk. This is a hardening weakness, not malicious behavior.",
      "layman_explanation": "The workflow runs a third-party tool using a version label instead of a locked commit. If that label were changed to point at bad code, the workflow would run it with significant repository permissions. Locking to a specific commit hash removes that risk.",
      "developer_action": "Pin wevm/frog/reconcile to a full commit SHA instead of a floating version tag, and review whether the id-token write permission is required for this step.",
